<div id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalized RGO from the proof of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. Its potential has Hessian between
<math id="S4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\eta)I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta)I</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimal transport
from the standard Gaussian to <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Caffarelli’s contraction theorem
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, applied in both directions, gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(1+\eta)^{-1/2}I\preceq DT_{y}\preceq I\,,\qquad\lVert DT_{y}-I\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant\eta/2\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="1.889em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta)^{-1/2}I\preceq DT_{y}\preceq I\,,\qquad\lVert DT_{y}-I\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant\eta/2\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">almost everywhere.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#A3.E22" title="Equation C.22 ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.22</span></a>), for <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)=-\eta^{-k}\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X\mid Y=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Cum</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)=-\eta^{-k}\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X\mid Y=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under the RGO,
<math id="S4.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}\,T_{y}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}\,T_{y}(G)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Translation invariance and homogeneity of
cumulants, followed by (<a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 4.10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>) and
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6 (Cumulants of a near-identity Gaussian image). ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a> with <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{T}\leqslant\eta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{T}\leqslant\eta/2</annotation></semantics></math>, prove
(<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 4.7 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>)–(<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>).
The case <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math> is <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Hessian bounds for the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>; integrating the
<math id="S4.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math> estimate (<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>) along a segment gives
(<a href="#S4.E9" title="Equation 4.9 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>